  "archetype": "a2-wire-cache-primed-unauth-control-spoof",
  "description": "R3-05 independent-review FP (Track A2 universal primitives, reviewer gemini-4-neon-high): an authenticated member (member_a) reads a shared logged-in announcement endpoint whose response body is identical to another member's (member_b) response, using an unauthenticated 401 request as cleanControl. Because Track A2 removed the brittle X-Cache: HIT header check in favor of victim-matched digest + control ablation, wire_framing_and_cache_differential / parser_cache_differential (cache_primed) MUST bind cleanControl to the same attacker principal and HTTP method as attackerProbe and reject unauthenticated 401 controls for authenticated probes, otherwise any shared authenticated endpoint confirms as cache bleed.",
